.TH COST\-DIFF 1 "2026-09" "cost-diff" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cost-diff \- diff two AWS Cost Explorer periods into what changed, and why
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cost-diff
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares two AWS Cost Explorer periods and reports the movers: which
services, accounts or usage types account for the difference, largest
first \(em rather than a total that went up by an unexplained amount.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-last\-month
The previous full month against the one before it.
.TP
.BI \-\-period " YYYY-MM"
The period to analyse.
.TP
.BI \-\-vs " YYYY-MM"
Baseline period. The default is the month before
.BR \-\-period .
.TP
.BI \-\-group " DIMENSION"
Cost Explorer dimension to group by; the default is SERVICE.
.TP
.BI \-\-metric " METRIC"
Cost Explorer metric. The
.B Net
metrics net out credits and refunds;
.B Amortized
spreads reserved-instance and Savings Plan cost over its term.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
How many movers to show (default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-threshold " N"
Ignore changes under N dollars (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-slack " WEBHOOK"
Post the report to Slack.
.TP
.B \-\-why
Drill into the biggest mover by usage type. Only meaningful with
.BR "\-\-group SERVICE" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A report was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
Cost Explorer could not be queried.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
What changed last month, and why:
.PP
.RS
.B cost-diff \-\-last\-month \-\-why
.RE
.PP
Two named months, posted to Slack:
.PP
.RS
.B cost-diff \-\-period 2026-06 \-\-vs 2026-05 \-\-slack "$WEBHOOK_URL"
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iam-shrink (1),
.BR idle-hunter (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/cost-diff
.UE
